# Project Conventions

Single Next.js app (not a monorepo). No `@netmifi/*` workspace packages here.

## Folders

- `app/` — routes, layouts, `loading.tsx` / `error.tsx`, route-only composition
- `components/` — reusable presentational UI
- `lib/` — `env`, utils, server helpers, data access
- `public/` — static files
- Config stays at repo root (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `biome.json`, `next.config.ts`)

Do not force a `src/` root; Next.js uses `app/` at the project root. When porting to mono, UI goes to `packages/design/src/` and logic to the matching package `src/`.

## Imports

```typescript
import { Button } from "@/components/button";
import type { Course } from "@/lib/types/course";
```

- Use `@/` instead of long relative paths
- `import type` for type-only imports
- Let Biome sort imports

## Runtime

- Bun only: `bun install`, `bun run`, `bun test` (`bun:test`)
- Tests: `*.test.ts` / `*.spec.ts`

## Environment

- Gitignore `.env*`; commit `.env.example`
- When env is needed, add a typed helper in `lib/env.ts` — do not read `process.env` throughout the app
- Browser-exposed vars: `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` only
